requirements.detail:
Establishes a performance code defining handle capabilities:
- Digit 1 (Category of Use): Grade 1 (Light Duty) up to Grade 4 (High Frequency/Heavy Duty);
- Digit 2 (Durability): Grade 4 (25,000 cycles) to Grade 7 (200,000 cycles of operation);
- Digit 3 (Test Door Mass): No classification (marked as '-');
- Digit 4 (Fire Resistance): Grade 0 (not suitable) up to fire-rated categories;
- Digit 5 (Safety): Grade 1 (essential safety-in-use requirements);
- Digit 6 (Types of Operation): Grade A (Spring assisted), Grade B (Spring loaded), Grade U (Un-sprung).
